          "literatureReview": "Protein electrophoresis separates serum proteins into albumin and globulin fractions. Normal: total protein 6.0-8.5 g/dL, albumin 3.5-5.0 g/dL, globulin 2.0-3.5 g/dL, A/G ratio 1.0-2.0. Abnormal patterns indicate liver disease, multiple myeloma, and immune deficiencies. Capillary electrophoresis provides high resolution. Critical for paraprotein detection and nutritional assessment."
